[b]QLC+ Swiss Knife v1.8.0 — meshes on the floor[/b]

A new release of Swiss Knife, the free companion toolkit for QLC+ 5 workspaces (not affiliated with the QLC+ project).

[b]Stage & Meshes[/b] places the 3D meshes of your show (band members, risers, truss…) by what you see:
[list]
[*]Plan and front views of the stage with fixtures and meshes; drag to move.
[*]Centre on the stage and height above the floor instead of QLC+'s raw numbers — which depend on how the model was drawn (a character with its feet at 0 needs Y −900 to stand on the floor).
[*]See which models float or sink; one click puts them all exactly on the floor.
[*]Rotate and scale keeping the model in place; add models from your folders, standing on the floor; change the stage keeping the meshes where they are.
[/list]
The wiki page also documents how QLC+ 5 stores and places meshes.

Your original show file is never changed — the result is saved as a new .qxw.

Download: [url=https://github.com/giopas/qlc-plus-swiss-knife-tool-script/releases/tag/v1.8.0]GitHub release v1.8.0[/url] · [url=https://github.com/giopas/qlc-plus-swiss-knife-tool-script/wiki]Wiki[/url]
